# REQUIRES: cuda, python-api, torch
# Force matching through mdir.torch (D382, #726 part E),
# on a GPU. Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py forms the product of
# D381 by autograd in its two forms: through the output
# gradients["positions"], and through the gradient of the energy taken with
# create_graph=True. Both must equal FrameEnergies.vjp, and the references
# of the scenarios of python_frame_product.py then check the result:
# closed forms and NumPy sums with their tangents, central differences, and
# mixed against double.
# Then gradcheck of the gradient in the positions in theta, in double; the
# refusals are those of python-frame-product-torch.test.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide dihedral GPU Double %t/dihedral | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIHEDRAL -DMODE="GPU Double torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide dihedral GPU Mixed %t/dihedral-mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIHEDRAL -DMODE="GPU Mixed torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide lj GPU Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LJ -DMODE="GPU Double torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide lj GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LJMIXED -DMODE="GPU Mixed torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide charges GPU Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHARGES -DMODE="GPU Double torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide charges GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CHARGES -DMODE="GPU Mixed torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_product_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide gradcheck GPU Double %t/gradcheck | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GRADCHECK -DMODE="GPU Double torch"

# DIHEDRAL: [[MODE]]: the product through mdir.torch (output) against FrameEnergies.vjp
# DIHEDRAL: [[MODE]]: the product through mdir.torch (create_graph) against FrameEnergies.vjp
# DIHEDRAL: [[MODE]]: dihedral_k, 3 frames, against the closed form along the cotangent
# DIHEDRAL: [[MODE]]: with a zero cotangent on the positions, against vjp(g) with the Jacobian
# LJ: [[MODE]]: the product through mdir.torch (create_graph) against FrameEnergies.vjp
# LJ: [[MODE]]: propane and water, per-type and pair sigma and epsilon with a pair set apart, 3 frames, against the NumPy sum
# LJ: [[MODE]]: the same against central differences of the rows along the cotangent
# LJMIXED: [[MODE]]: the product through mdir.torch (create_graph) against FrameEnergies.vjp
# LJMIXED: [[MODE]]: propane and water, per-type and pair sigma and epsilon with a pair set apart, 3 frames, against the NumPy sum
# LJMIXED: [[MODE]]: the product in mixed precision against that in double
# CHARGES: [[MODE]]: the product through mdir.torch (create_graph) against FrameEnergies.vjp
# CHARGES: [[MODE]]: the charges under a Coulomb cutoff, 25 entries for 1168 particles, 2 frames, against the NumPy sum
# GRADCHECK: [[MODE]]: gradcheck of the gradient in the positions in theta (output): dihedral_k on the torsion fixtures, passed
# GRADCHECK: [[MODE]]: gradcheck of the gradient in the positions in theta (create_graph): dihedral_k on the torsion fixtures, passed
# GRADCHECK: [[MODE]]: gradcheck of the gradient in the positions in theta (output): sigma and epsilon of two pairs of types on propane and water, passed
# GRADCHECK: [[MODE]]: gradcheck of the gradient in the positions in theta (create_graph): sigma and epsilon of two pairs of types on propane and water, passed
